  <section id="overview">
    <h2 class="section-title">Research Overview</h2>

    <div class="card">
      <p>
        Virtual Reality (VR) creates fully immersive digital environments, 
        while Augmented Reality (AR) overlays digital information onto the real world. 
        The development of <span class="highlight">6G communication networks</span> is expected 
        to dramatically improve these technologies through ultra-fast data transfer, 
        extremely low latency, artificial intelligence integration, and real-time processing.
      </p>

      <br>

      <p>
        Our research focuses on how AI-driven communication infrastructure and 
        6G wireless networks can enable immersive AR/VR collaboration platforms 
        and reshape global work structures by 2040.
      </p>

      <div class="quote">
        “6G is presented as a next generation network capable of delivering high data speeds, 
        ultra-low latency, and more reliable connectivity than current networks.”
        <br><br>
        — EST 320 Group 7 Book Review Assignment
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="6g">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Role of 6G Communication</h2>

    <div class="grid">

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Ultra-Low Latency</h3>
        <p>
          Immersive VR and AR systems require near-instant responses to maintain realism.
          6G networks aim to reduce latency significantly beyond 5G capabilities,
          allowing smoother interaction in virtual environments.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>High Data Speeds</h3>
        <p>
          6G communication may support terabyte-level data transfer rates,
          enabling high-quality graphics, real-time simulations,
          and large-scale virtual collaboration.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Edge Computing</h3>
        <p>
          Edge computing allows data processing closer to users,
          reducing delays and improving real-time performance
          for immersive applications and AI systems.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="applications">
    <h2 class="section-title">Applications of VR & AR</h2>

    <div class="grid">

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Education</h3>
        <p>
          VR and AR can create interactive classrooms, virtual laboratories,
          and immersive learning environments that increase engagement and accessibility.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Healthcare</h3>
        <p>
          Medical students may use VR simulations for surgical training,
          while AR can provide doctors with real-time patient information
          during medical procedures.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Remote Work</h3>
        <p>
          Future collaboration systems could allow employees to interact in shared
          virtual offices rather than traditional video conferencing platforms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Entertainment & Gaming</h3>
        <p>
          VR gaming and immersive entertainment experiences continue to expand,
          supported by faster networking and improved graphics rendering.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="quote">
      “VR provides an immersive gaming experience, transporting users to virtual worlds 
      where they can explore, interact, and compete.”
      <br><br>
      — Sundaravadivazhagan, Chapter 11
    </div>

  </section>

  <section id="ai">
    <h2 class="section-title">Artificial Intelligence Integration</h2>

    <div class="card">
      <p>
        Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning (ML), and Deep Learning (DL)
        are critical for future immersive systems. AI allows VR and AR platforms
        to process visual and spatial information, interpret user behavior,
        and generate adaptive virtual environments in real time.
      </p>

      <br>

      <p>
        AI-powered avatars, virtual assistants, and smart environments
        may improve communication, education, customer support,
        and workplace collaboration.
      </p>

      <div class="quote">
        “AI models allow virtual environments to respond more naturally 
        to user behavior and their surroundings.”
        <br><br>
        — EST 320 Book Review
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="challenges">
    <h2 class="section-title">Challenges & Ethical Concerns</h2>

    <div class="grid">

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Privacy & Security</h3>
        <p>
          Immersive systems collect significant amounts of personal data,
          including facial expressions, body movement, and voice information.
          Protecting this data remains a major challenge.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Accessibility</h3>
        <p>
          High equipment costs and infrastructure limitations may prevent
          equal access to immersive technologies worldwide.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Mental Health</h3>
        <p>
          Researchers continue to examine how long-term use of immersive environments
          may affect social behavior, attention, and psychological well-being.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Technical Limitations</h3>
        <p>
          Current issues include bulky hardware, motion sickness,
          tracking inaccuracies, energy consumption,
          and the need for large-scale infrastructure development.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="future">
    <h2 class="section-title">Future Impact by 2040</h2>

    <div class="card">
      <p>
        By 2040, immersive AR and VR systems supported by 6G communication
        may significantly change how people work, learn, and interact globally.
        Virtual collaboration platforms could replace many traditional online meetings,
        while AI-powered environments may allow realistic simulations
        for healthcare, manufacturing, engineering, and education.
      </p>

      <br>

      <p>
        Researchers also believe these technologies may contribute to
        decentralized global work structures, allowing professionals
        from different countries to collaborate in immersive digital spaces
        with minimal communication barriers.
      </p>

      <div class="quote">
        “The combination of immersive technologies and advanced communication networks
        will likely play an important role in shaping the future of learning,
        entertainment, and human interaction.”
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

